{"labs": [{"id": 0, "type": "scholar", "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "title": "", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn7le17ob07re2img03.jpg"}, {"text": "Environmental organizations were horrified by the most recent report on the state of Lake Kachanawa. The pollution levels are unprecedented, and thousands of gallons of hazardous waste materials are being poured into its waters every day.", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn7le17ob07re2img03.jpg"}, {"text": "In recent years, a new type of alga has appeared in the lake. This poisonous parasite was first introduced by the increased amount of noxious bacteria released into the waters. Research was conducted regarding its long-term effect. The results are clear: if we keep the lake in its current state, we will face an ecological disaster of catastrophic proportions. We will witness the death of a natural wonder within our lifetime if we don't change the way we live right now.", "id": 2, "time": "16500", "image": "engenn7le17ob07re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "To make matters worse, regulations regarding pollution were never properly carried out by any governing body. Although warnings were given to offenders, they were never taken seriously. If the perpetrators were fined or jailed, maybe things would change.", "id": 3, "time": "47800", "image": "engenn7le17ob07re2img02.jpg"}, {"text": "Not enough is being done to protect the waters of Lake Kachanawa. The purity of this beautiful lake was never taken for granted by our ancestors. If they could see us now, they would be appalled by what Lake Kachanawa has become. People will flee and wildlife will perish if we don't safeguard this important water source.", "id": 4, "time": "63800", "image": "engenn7le17ob07re2img03.jpg"}], "audiosrc": "engenn7le17ob07re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn7le17ob07re2img03.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "_data": [], "type